{
  "dom_id": "step-q146184",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "| $x$ | $2$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0)$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ |\n\nFind the $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=0]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0)$ is shown in the table above.",
  "worked_solution": "The conditional expected value of  $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=0] & ={\\sum }_{x}x\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}+5\\cdot \\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{3} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
